      "message": "`SendBootromCommandSha` and `SendBootromCommandAes` duplicate the logic for validating `SecureResponseHeader`, handling truncation, and extracting the payload length.\n\n**The Fix:** Extract the common response parsing into a private helper in `BootromComm`:\n\n```c\nstd::expected\u003cstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e BootromComm::ExtractSecurePayload(\n    std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e raw_response, size_t min_resp_size) {\n    \n  auto rsp_hdr_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cSecureResponseHeader\u003e(raw_response);\n  if (!rsp_hdr_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  \n  uint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d FromLittleEndian(rsp_hdr_res-\u003epayload_len);\n  if (rsp_wrapped_len \u003e raw_response.size() - min_resp_size) {\n    rsp_wrapped_len \u003d raw_response.size() - min_resp_size;\n  }\n  \n  return raw_response.subspan(sizeof(SecureResponseHeader), rsp_wrapped_len);\n}\n\n```\n\nYou can then call this inside both `Sha` and `Aes` command handlers, drastically reducing their visual footprint.",
