      "message": "Here are the Gemini-generated steps to fix this. Verify it\u0027s correct:\n\n---\n\nHere are the exact steps to implement the \"Unify Secure Response Parsing\" refactor. This will eliminate the duplicate header parsing and bounds-checking logic from both cryptographic command functions.\n\n### **Step 1: Declare the helper in `bootrom.h**`\n\nAdd the `ExtractSecureData` helper method to the `private` section of the `BootromComm` class.\n\n```cpp\n// In util/egis/bootrom.h\n\n private:\n  // ... existing private members ...\n\n  std::expected\u003cstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e ExtractSecureData(\n      std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e raw_response, size_t min_resp_size);\n\n```\n\n### **Step 2: Implement the helper in `bootrom.cc**`\n\nThis helper will read the header, check for truncation, handle endianness, safely clamp the payload length to avoid out-of-bounds reads, and return a span of all the data immediately following the header.\n\n```cpp\n// In util/egis/bootrom.cc (Add this near your other DoUsbTransfer/Send methods)\n\nstd::expected\u003cstd::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e, BootromError\u003e \nBootromComm::ExtractSecureData(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e raw_response, \n                               size_t min_resp_size) {\n  auto rsp_hdr_res \u003d ReadStruct\u003cSecureResponseHeader\u003e(raw_response);\n  if (!rsp_hdr_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n\n  uint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d FromLittleEndian(rsp_hdr_res-\u003epayload_len);\n\n  // Clamp the payload length based on the actual bytes received\n  if (rsp_wrapped_len \u003e raw_response.size() - min_resp_size) {\n    rsp_wrapped_len \u003d raw_response.size() - min_resp_size;\n  }\n\n  // Calculate the size of the non-payload data (e.g., IV + Tag for AES)\n  size_t extra_data_size \u003d min_resp_size - sizeof(SecureResponseHeader);\n\n  // Return a safe subspan covering everything after the header\n  return raw_response.subspan(sizeof(SecureResponseHeader), \n                              extra_data_size + rsp_wrapped_len);\n}\n\n```\n\n### **Step 3: Clean up `SendBootromCommandSha**`\n\nReplace the manual parsing and bounds-checking logic with the new helper. Notice how much boilerplate this removes.\n\n**Before:**\n\n```cpp\n  auto ret_res \u003d DoUsbTransfer(cmd, sizeof(SecureResponseHeader), timeout);\n  if (!ret_res) return std::unexpected(ret_res.error());\n  auto \u0026ret \u003d ret_res.value();\n\n  auto rsp_hdr_res \u003d\n      ReadStruct\u003cSecureResponseHeader\u003e(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e(ret));\n  if (!rsp_hdr_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  SecureResponseHeader rsp_hdr \u003d rsp_hdr_res.value();\n\n  uint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d FromLittleEndian(rsp_hdr.payload_len);\n  if (rsp_wrapped_len \u003e ret.size() - sizeof(SecureResponseHeader)) {\n    rsp_wrapped_len \u003d ret.size() - sizeof(SecureResponseHeader);\n  }\n\n  auto rsp_payload \u003d std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e(ret).subspan(\n      sizeof(SecureResponseHeader), rsp_wrapped_len);\n\n  return std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e(rsp_payload.begin(), rsp_payload.end());\n\n```\n\n**After:**\n\n```cpp\n  auto ret_res \u003d DoUsbTransfer(cmd, sizeof(SecureResponseHeader), timeout);\n  if (!ret_res) return std::unexpected(ret_res.error());\n\n  auto rsp_payload \u003d ExtractSecureData(ret_res.value(), sizeof(SecureResponseHeader));\n  if (!rsp_payload) return std::unexpected(rsp_payload.error());\n\n  return std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e(rsp_payload-\u003ebegin(), rsp_payload-\u003eend());\n\n```\n\n### **Step 4: Clean up `SendBootromCommandAes**`\n\nDo the same for the AES function. Because AES includes the IV and Tag immediately after the header, we pass the larger `min_resp_size`. We also apply the earlier security fix: decrypting into a distinct vector instead of decrypting in-place to prevent pointer aliasing.\n\n**Before:**\n\n```cpp\n  size_t min_resp_size \u003d\n      sizeof(SecureResponseHeader) + kAesGcmIvSize + kAesGcmTagSize;\n  auto ret_res \u003d DoUsbTransfer(cmd, min_resp_size, timeout);\n  if (!ret_res) return std::unexpected(ret_res.error());\n  auto \u0026ret \u003d ret_res.value();\n\n  auto rsp_hdr_res \u003d\n      ReadStruct\u003cSecureResponseHeader\u003e(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e(ret));\n  if (!rsp_hdr_res) return std::unexpected(BootromError::kResponseTruncated);\n  SecureResponseHeader rsp_hdr \u003d rsp_hdr_res.value();\n\n  uint32_t rsp_wrapped_len \u003d FromLittleEndian(rsp_hdr.payload_len);\n  if (rsp_wrapped_len \u003e ret.size() - min_resp_size) {\n    rsp_wrapped_len \u003d ret.size() - min_resp_size;\n  }\n\n  std::span\u003cuint8_t\u003e ret_span \u003d ret;\n  size_t offset \u003d sizeof(SecureResponseHeader);\n  auto rsp_iv \u003d ret_span.subspan(offset, kAesGcmIvSize);\n  offset +\u003d kAesGcmIvSize;\n  auto rsp_tag \u003d ret_span.subspan(offset, kAesGcmTagSize);\n  offset +\u003d kAesGcmTagSize;\n  auto rsp_payload \u003d ret_span.subspan(offset, rsp_wrapped_len);\n\n  if (auto res \u003d crypto::AesGcmDecrypt(aes_key_, rsp_iv, aad_span, rsp_payload,\n                                       rsp_tag, rsp_payload);\n      !res) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Decryption Failed: {}\",\n                 crypto::ToString(res.error()));\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kGcmAuthenticationFailed);\n  }\n\n  return std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e(rsp_payload.begin(), rsp_payload.end());\n\n```\n\n**After (Integrating the crypto constants fix as well):**\n\n```cpp\n  size_t min_resp_size \u003d sizeof(SecureResponseHeader) + \n                         crypto::kAesGcmIvSize + crypto::kAesGcmTagSize;\n  \n  auto ret_res \u003d DoUsbTransfer(cmd, min_resp_size, timeout);\n  if (!ret_res) return std::unexpected(ret_res.error());\n\n  auto secure_data \u003d ExtractSecureData(ret_res.value(), min_resp_size);\n  if (!secure_data) return std::unexpected(secure_data.error());\n\n  // secure_data now perfectly encompasses exactly [IV][Tag][Payload]\n  size_t offset \u003d 0;\n  auto rsp_iv \u003d secure_data-\u003esubspan(offset, crypto::kAesGcmIvSize);\n  offset +\u003d crypto::kAesGcmIvSize;\n  \n  auto rsp_tag \u003d secure_data-\u003esubspan(offset, crypto::kAesGcmTagSize);\n  offset +\u003d crypto::kAesGcmTagSize;\n  \n  auto rsp_ciphertext \u003d secure_data-\u003esubspan(offset);\n\n  // Decrypt into a fresh vector to avoid pointer aliasing vulnerabilities\n  std::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e decrypted_payload(rsp_ciphertext.size());\n\n  if (auto res \u003d crypto::AesGcmDecrypt(aes_key_, rsp_iv, aad_span, rsp_ciphertext,\n                                       rsp_tag, decrypted_payload);\n      !res) {\n    std::println(stderr, \"[ERROR] Decryption Failed: {}\",\n                 crypto::ToString(res.error()));\n    return std::unexpected(BootromError::kGcmAuthenticationFailed);\n  }\n\n  return decrypted_payload;\n\n```",
