      "message": "In `egis_util.h`, `ReadStruct` returns `std::expected\u003cT, std::errc\u003e`, but `ReadLittleEndian` returns `std::optional\u003cT\u003e`.\n\nAccording to Google C++ Style, you should prefer `std::expected` when the reason for failure is actionable or needs to be logged, and `std::optional` only when the absence of a value is a normal, expected state. Since reading past the end of a buffer is an error state, make them consistent.\n\n**The Fix:** Change `ReadLittleEndian` to return `std::expected\u003cT, std::errc\u003e`:\n\n```c\ntemplate \u003cstd::integral T\u003e\nstd::expected\u003cT, std::errc\u003e ReadLittleEndian(std::span\u003cconst uint8_t\u003e buffer) {\n  if (buffer.size() \u003c sizeof(T)) return std::unexpected(std::errc::message_size);\n\n  T value;\n  std::memcpy(\u0026value, buffer.data(), sizeof(T));\n  return FromLittleEndian(value);\n}\n\n```",
